.el .ds Aq '
.TH tapectl-cartridge-register 1  "tapectl-cartridge-register " 
.SH NAME
tapectl\-cartridge\-register \- Register a physical cartridge
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtapectl cartridge register\fR <\fB\-\-barcode\fR> [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] <\fB\-\-media\-type\fR> [\fB\-\-capacity\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-serial\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-notes\fR] [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Register a physical cartridge
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-barcode\fR \fI<BARCODE>\fR
Barcode label
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output in JSON format
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be done without making changes
.TP
\fB\-\-media\-type\fR \fI<MEDIA_TYPE>\fR
Media generation (e.g., LTO\-6, LTO\-7, LTO\-7\-M8, LTO\-8)
.TP
\fB\-\-capacity\fR \fI<CAPACITY>\fR
Nominal capacity, e.g. "2500G". Defaults to the generation table\*(Aqs marketed figure (ADR\-0010) when omitted — give this explicitly only when the physical cartridge really differs (a declared 40 TB LTO\-10 cartridge, an mhvtl micro\-tape, ...)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose output
.TP
\fB\-\-serial\fR \fI<SERIAL>\fR
Medium serial number (MAM), if already known — `volume init` records this itself when it auto\-registers or matches a cartridge from a loaded tape\*(Aqs MAM; set it by hand only when pre\-registering a cartridge that has not been loaded yet
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip confirmation prompts
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to config file.

NOTE: on its own this ALSO relocates the whole tapectl home to the config file\*(Aqs parent directory — database, keys, staging, receipts. That is how every test harness gets an isolated home, so it still works, but it is surprising enough that it now warns. Use \-\-home when you mean "operate on a different archive", and \-\-config only to point at a config file inside that home (issue #109).
.TP
\fB\-\-notes\fR \fI<NOTES>\fR
Notes
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<HOME>\fR
tapectl home directory: database, keys, catalogs, receipts, logs.

Defaults to ~/.tapectl. The config file is taken from <home>/config.toml unless \-\-config overrides it. Also settable as TAPECTL_HOME (issue #109).
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
